From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmcompos: chord map Load and GetScale, chord map track and signpost track data, ChangeChordMap, template object

The chord map, the chord map track, the signpost track and the template object were stubs. Now:
- the chord map loads its 'perh' chunk (scale pattern; the chord and signpost data is used by the composer only and is not kept)
  and GetScale returns the pattern (E_POINTER without a pointer);
- the chord map track keeps chord maps by time (SetParam/GetParam GUID_IDirectMusicChordMap, the one in effect with the time
  until the next one; DMUS_E_NOT_FOUND when empty), Load of a LIST 'cmap' holding a chord map form or a reference, Clone
  ([start,end) moved to zero, the chord map in effect carried), Join, the extended methods through the play state of InitPlay,
  and the argument checks (E_POINTER) the tests expect;
- the signpost track keeps its signposts: Load/Save of the 'sgnp' chunk, Clone, Join, notification types (E_POINTER without a
  type, S_FALSE), PlayEx; GetParam/SetParam/IsParamSupported and the extended methods stay E_NOTIMPL as the tests show;
  Compose logs a FIXME (the chord progression is not composed);
- IDirectMusicComposer::ChangeChordMap puts the chord map into the chord map tracks of the segment (adding a track when there is
  none) and, with the track scale flag, gives every chord its scale;
- the template object can be created (IPersistStream; Load is E_NOTIMPL).
The todo_wine marks of the tests which pass are removed. The composer's ComposeSegmentFromTemplate/Shape, ComposeTransition,
AutoTransition and ComposeTemplateFromShape need a chord progression engine and are unchanged.
